{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Nevertheless, let Kain be for a burning, etc.</b> Fortunate are you that you are driven into this stronghold — that you are never again banished from the world. For even though you are destined to go into exile with the ten tribes, and be swept away from the place where you settled — what of it?" "<b>Until what point shall Asshur take you captive.</b> To where does He reveal you? Perhaps to Halah and Habor? That is not banishment from the world, but wandering from place to place — and you shall return with the rest of the exiles."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:39.221357742Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}